 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2022-09-29",
   "text": "Mandatory Materiality Requirement Act of 2022 \n This bill limits additional disclosure requirements applicable to issuers of securities. Specifically, the Securities and Exchange Commission may only require an additional disclosure if the commission determines that there is a substantial likelihood that a reasonable investor of the issuer would consider the information important with respect to an investment decision."
  }
